---
/*
 * SoCraTes BE head additions (dk:head slot). Advertises the page's machine
 * views as <link rel="alternate">, next to the RSS and llms.txt links the
 * toolkit adds to every page, so an agent reading the head finds them.
 *
 * A theme's dk:head replaces the toolkit's default, so this renders that
 * default (HeadShare, the og:image / twitter:image metadata) first, with the
 * props the toolkit's Head carrier passes it. This theme sets no
 * `assets.socialImage`, so HeadShare's own site default applies.
 */
import type { Props as StarlightRoute } from '@astrojs/starlight/props';
import HeadShare from '@spec-kitty/doc-toolkit/components/slots/HeadShare.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { slugFromEntryId } from '@spec-kitty/doc-toolkit';
import { viewLinks, viewSlug } from '../lib/page-views';

const route = (Astro.locals as unknown as { starlightRoute: StarlightRoute }).starlightRoute;
const data = route.entry.data as unknown as {
  title?: string;
  hero_image?: { src: string; alt: string };
  social_thumb?: { src: string; alt: string } | string;
};
const filePath = (route.entry as unknown as { filePath?: string }).filePath;

// Only docs entries have machine views (see SiteFooter.astro for the matching).
const entry = (await getCollection('docs')).find(
  (e) => slugFromEntryId(e.id) === slugFromEntryId(route.entry.id),
);
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const views = entry ? viewLinks(base, viewSlug(entry.id)) : undefined;
const alternates = views
  ? [
      { ...views.json, title: 'This page as JSON' },
      { ...views.yaml, title: 'This page as YAML' },
      { ...views.markdown, title: 'This page as Markdown' },
    ]
  : [];
---

<HeadShare
  heroImage={data.hero_image}
  socialThumb={data.social_thumb}
  filePath={filePath}
  title={data.title}
  siteTitle={route.siteTitle}
/>
{alternates.map((link) => <link rel="alternate" type={link.type} title={link.title} href={link.href} />)}
